  volume       = {169},
  pages        = {107164},
  date         = {2020-03},
  abstract     = {Karl Lashley began the search for the engram nearly seventy
                  years ago. In the time since, much has been learned but
                  divisions remain. In the contemporary neurobiology of learning
                  and memory, two profoundly different conceptions contend: the
                  associative/connectionist (A/C) conception and the
