  abstract     = {Since the work of Ramón y Cajal in the late 19th and early
                  20th centuries, neuroscientists have speculated that a
                  complete understanding of neuronal cell types and their
                  connections is key to explaining complex brain functions.
                  However, a complete census of the constituent cell types and
                  their wiring diagram in mature neocortex remains elusive. By
                  combining octuple whole-cell recordings with an optimized
                  avidin-biotin-peroxidase staining technique, we carried out a
                  morphological and electrophysiological census of neuronal
                  types in layers 1, 2/3, and 5 of mature neocortex and mapped
                  the connectivity between more than 11,000 pairs of identified
                  neurons. We categorized 15 types of interneurons, and each
