                  other contaminants on SARS-CoV-2 has been poorly explored.
                  Here we examined the possible reasons why the new coronavirus
                  differently impacted on Italian regional and provincial
                  populations. With the help of artificial intelligence, we
                  studied the importance of air pollution for mortality and
                  positivity rates of the SARS-CoV-2 outbreak in Italy. We
                  discovered that among several environmental, health, and
                  socio-economic factors, air pollution and fine particulate
                  matter (PM2.5), as its main component, resulted as the most
                  important predictors of SARS-CoV-2 effects. We also found that
