                  score at 1-year follow-up and the two conditions were
                  correlated (r = 0.72, P < 0.001). Compared to the natural
                  progression of motor disability, levodopa treatment resulted
                  in a 31\% lower annual decline in UPDRS-III scores in the OFF
                  state (3.33 versus 2.30 points/year) with a lower model’s
