                  implicating several neuromodulator systems. This review
                  considers a new approach based on existing theories of
                  functional brain organisation. The free energy principle
                  (a.k.a. active inference), and its instantiation in the
                  Bayesian brain, offers a complete and simple formulation of
                  mood. It has been proposed that emotions reflect the precision
                  of – or certainty about – the predicted
                  sensorimotor/interoceptive consequences of action. By
                  extending this reasoning, in a hierarchical setting, we
                  suggest mood states act as (hyper) priors over uncertainty
