  date         = {2020},
  abstract     = {Reinforcement learning (RL) is a framework of particular
                  importance to psychology, neuroscience and machine learning.
                  Interactions between these fields, as promoted through the
                  common hub of RL, has facilitated paradigm shifts that relate
                  multiple levels of analysis in a singular framework (for
                  example, relating dopamine function to a computationally
