                  decision-making. Here, we outline some of the consequences
                  that come from overconfidently mapping algorithms, such as MB
                  versus MF RL, with putative cognitive processes. We argue that
                  the field is well positioned to move beyond simplistic
                  dichotomies, and we propose a means of refocusing research
                  questions towards the rich and complex components that
                  comprise learning and decision-making. Reinforcement learning
                  has been suggested to come in two flavours: model-free and
