  pages        = {2020.10.24.353409},
  date         = {2020},
  abstract     = {The search for biologically faithful synaptic plasticity rules
                  has resulted in a large body of models. They are usually
                  inspired by – and fitted to – experimental data, but they
                  rarely produce neural dynamics that serve complex functions.
                  These failures suggest that current plasticity models are
                  still under-constrained by existing data. Here, we present an
                  alternative approach that uses meta-learning to discover
