                  activity, we find unexpected similarities at the neural
                  population level: the structure and activity of the neural
                  modes is largely preserved across tasks. Furthermore, we find
                  two sets of neural modes with task-independent activity that
                  capture, respectively, generic temporal features of the set of
                  tasks and a task-independent mapping onto muscle activity.
                  This system of flexibly combined, well-preserved neural modes
