                  apparent divide between the physically incoherent
                  consciousness we think we have and the complex, rich, but
                  mechanistic consciousness we may actually have. We suggest
                  this approach helps reconcile some of the current cognitive
                  neuroscience theories of consciousness. We argue that a
                  single, coherent explanation of consciousness is available and
                  has been for some time, encompassing the views of many
