  date         = {2020},
  abstract     = {Mental accounting refers to the fact that people create mental
                  budgets to organize their resource use and to create linkages
                  between specific acts of consumption and specific payments.
                  Research on financial decision-making and consumer behaviour
                  shows that these mechanisms can have a large impact on
