  pages        = {1022--1030},
  date         = {2019},
  abstract     = {Patients with functional movement disorders also typically
                  have functional somatic symptoms, including pain, fatigue, and
                  sensory disturbance. A potentially unifying mechanism for such
                  symptoms is a failure in processing of sensory inputs.
                  Prepulse inhibition is a neurophysiological method that allows
                  for the study of preconscious somatosensory processing. The
                  objective of this study was to assess prepulse inhibition in
                  patients with functional movement disorders and healthy
                  control subjects. We analyzed the effect of a weak electrical
                  stimulus to the index finger (prepulse) on the magnitude of
                  the R2 response of the blink reflex induced by electrical
