  journaltitle = {arXiv},
  date         = {2018},
  abstract     = {Latent variable models have been widely applied for the
                  analysis of time series resulting from experimental
                  neuroscience techniques. In these datasets, observations are
                  relatively smooth and possibly nonlinear. We present
                  Variational Inference for Nonlinear Dynamics (VIND), a
                  variational inference framework that is able to uncover
                  nonlinear, smooth latent dynamics from sequential data. The
                  framework is a direct extension of PfLDS; including a
                  structured approximate posterior describing
                  spatially-dependent linear dynamics, as well as an algorithm
                  that relies on the fixed-point iteration method to achieve
                  convergence. We apply VIND to electrophysiology, single-cell
                  voltage and widefield imaging datasets with state-of-the-art
