  date         = {2009},
  abstract     = {We review and synthesize recent neurophysiological studies of
                  decision making in humans and nonhuman primates. From these
                  studies, the basic outline of the neurobiological mechanism
                  for primate choice is beginning to emerge. The identified
                  mechanism is now known to include a multicomponent valuation
                  stage, implemented in ventromedial prefrontal cortex and
