  abstract     = {Gambling disorder is characterized by persistent and recurrent
                  maladaptive gambling behavior, which leads to clinically
                  significant impairment or distress. The disorder is associated
                  with dysfunctions in the dopamine system. The dopamine system
                  codes reward anticipation and outcome evaluation. Reward
                  anticipation refers to dopaminergic activation prior to
                  reward, while outcome evaluation refers to dopaminergic
