  pages        = {47--52},
  date         = {2012},
  abstract     = {After entering the cerebral cortex, sensory information
                  spreads through six different horizontal neuronal layers that
                  are interconnected by vertical axonal projections. It is
                  believed that through these projections layers can influence
                  each other's response to sensory stimuli, but the specific
                  role that each layer has in cortical processing is still
