                  APAP metabolites N-arachidonoylaminophenol (AM404) and
                  N-acetyl-p-benzoquinone imine (NAPQI) have been detected in
                  the central nervous system after systemic APAP administration
                  and were reported to mediate paracetamol effects. In contrast
                  to NSAIDs which rather support seizure activity, paracetamol
                  provides anticonvulsant actions, and this dampening of
