                  undergoing functional magnetic resonance imaging. This work
                  suggests that ventromedial and lateral prefrontal cortex and
                  orbitofrontal cortex are important for forming value judgments
                  under conditions of complexity. We discuss studies supporting
                  the involvement of these regions in selecting among and
                  evaluating option attributes during value judgment and
                  decision-making and when learning from reward feedback. These
