  pages        = {1--10},
  date         = {2020},
  abstract     = {Addiction was suggested to emerge from the progressive
                  dominance of habits over goal-directed behaviors. However, it
                  is generally assumed that habits do not persist in choice
                  settings. Therefore, it is unclear how drug habits may persist
                  in real-world scenarios where this factor predominates. Here,
                  we discuss the poor translational validity of the habit
                  construct, which impedes our ability to determine its role in
