                  unknown. Fifteen adult ET patients received a single oral
                  ethanol dose calculated to reach 0.05 g/dL breath alcohol
                  content (brAC). Effects were investigated independently with
                  accelerometry and TETRAS. Accelerometry data were
                  log-transformed and a cumulative score logACC(R+L) was
