  abstract  = {Predictive processing accounts of neural function view the brain
               as a kind of prediction machine that forms models of its
               environment in order to anticipate the upcoming stream of sensory
               stimulation. These models are then continuously updated in light
               of incoming error signals. Predictive processing has offered a
               powerful new perspective on cognition, action, and perception. In
