                  neuronal activity can improve symptoms of movement disorders
                  like Parkinson’s disease, tremor or dystonia. More than
                  160,000 patients worldwide have undergone DBS surgery so far,
                  with Parkinson’s disease being the most common indication.
                  This combined experience has sharpened knowledge on patient
                  selection, outcomes and risks. Not only movement disorders but
                  also epilepsy and certain neuropsychiatric disorders like
                  Tourette can be treated with DBS. There have been reports of
                  positive effects in several other neurological and psychiatric
                  disorders. In these cases, the procedure still has to be
                  regarded as more or less experimental. The following essay is
