                  recording ratings of valence and arousal to low- and
                  high-intensity positive and negative emotional images. STN
                  stimulation increased positive ratings and decreased negative
                  ratings to low-intensity positive and negative stimuli,
                  respectively, relative to off stimulation. We also show that
                  the change in severity of obsessive–compulsive symptoms pre-
                  versus post-operatively interacts with both DBS and valence
                  ratings. We show that stimulation of the associative-limbic
                  STN might influence the negative cognitive bias in OCD and
