  pages        = {111--143},
  date         = {2019},
  abstract     = {Parkinson's disease (PD) is a degenerative disorder of the
                  brain characterized by the impairment of the nigrostriatal
                  system. This impairment leads to specific motor manifestations
                  (i.e., bradykinesia, tremor, and rigidity) that are assessed
                  through clinical examination, scales, and patient-reported
                  outcomes. New sensor-based and wearable technologies are
