  pages        = {40--48},
  date         = {2016},
  abstract     = {To determine the clinical and demographic correlates of
                  persistent, remitting, and new-onset impulse control behaviors
                  (ICBs) before and after subthalamic deep brain stimulation
                  (STN-DBS) in Parkinson’s disease (PD). We compared the pre-
                  and post-surgical prevalence of ICBs, classified as impulse
                  control disorders (ICD), dopamine dysregulation syndrome
                  (DDS), and punding in 150 consecutive PD STN-DBS-treated
