                  areas in the dorsal visual stream. Here we examine whether
                  such convergence occurs subcortically in the macaque thalamus.
                  We searched the ventral posterior nuclei, including the
                  anterior pulvinar, as well as the ventro-lateral and ventral
                  posterior lateral nuclei, areas that receive vestibular
                  signals from brain stem and deep cerebellar nuclei.
                  Approximately a quarter of cells responded to
                  three-dimensional (3D) translational and/or rotational motion.
                  More than half of the responsive cells were convergent, thus
