                  on the EMG profile during standardized extension and flexion
                  movements in the elbow joint. These data correlate
                  significantly with clinical ratings. Thus, EMG recordings of
                  the Mm. bic and tric during this standardized
                  extension‐flexion movement can be used to objectively measure
                  rigidity and to monitor its course over time. In view of its
