  pages        = {85},
  date         = {2012},
  abstract     = {Dopamine has a central role in motivation and reward.
                  Dopaminergic neurons in the ventral tegmental area (VTA)
                  signal the discrepancy between expected and actual rewards
                  (that is, reward prediction error)1,2,3, but how they compute
                  such signals is unknown. We recorded the activity of VTA
