  date         = {1990},
  abstract     = {Although it is known that Parkinson's disease results from a
                  loss of dopaminergic neurons in the substantia nigra, the
                  resulting alterations in activity in the basal ganglia
                  responsible for parkinsonian motor deficits are still poorly
                  characterized. Recently, increased activity in the subthalamic
