  date      = {2015-04-30},
  abstract  = {Bayesian data analysis involves describing data by meaningful
               mathematical models, and allocating credibility to parameter
               values that are consistent with the data and with prior
               knowledge. The Bayesian approach is ideally suited for
               constructing hierarchical models, which are useful for data
               structures with multiple levels, such as data from individuals
               who are members of groups which in turn are in higher-level
               organizations. Hierarchical models have parameters that
               meaningfully describe the data at their multiple levels and
