  issue        = {11},
  pages        = {1857--1865},
  date         = {2017-11},
  abstract     = {Children with autism spectrum disorders (ASD) often show
                  changes in (automatic) auditory processing. Electrophysiology
                  provides a method to study auditory processing, by
                  investigating event-related potentials such as mismatch
                  negativity (MMN) and P3a-amplitude. However, findings on MMN
