  date         = {2009-05-01},
  abstract     = {Appropriate technologies (AT) are only a fraction of the
                  solution in achieving sustainable and safe access to water and
                  sanitation worldwide. The challenges of rapid population
                  increases, urbanization, climate change, poverty, and
                  widespread diseases will affect what are deemed “appropriate”
                  solutions in addressing needs in the water and sanitation
                  sector. Traditional engineering approaches need to be
                  augmented with more flexible trial and error techniques, user
