                  and predicted class-labels as output. The most extreme
                  cognitive scores were selected for class differentiation, i.e.
                  best vs. worst cognitive performance (n = 20 per group).
                  16,674 features were extracted per patient; feature-selection
                  was performed using a Boruta algorithm. A random forest
