               rescaled range analysis method, Higuchi's fractal dimension
               method, Approximate entropy method to quantize the gait dynamics
               of people suffering from Parkinson diseases (PD). Also they are
               asked to perform `Dual task' while walking, to have a better
               understanding of the connection between central nervous system
               and the limb movement. Gait dynamics of normal healthy people are
               also included in this study as control group. They are also put
               under study to perform dual task. This data set has been acquired
               from MIT-BIH data base. All these methods are capable to detect
               the difference between `Normal walking' and `Dual tasking' for
               both the groups. The fractal exponents for `Dual task' however
               produce interesting findings for PD subjects, suggesting that
