                  evaluate and select their niches. Well-developed theories of
                  both adaptive phenotypic plasticity and adaptive genetic
                  variation in the stress-response systems have been advanced in
                  the literature. Taken together, these theories strongly
                  suggest that variation in stress-response phenotypes has been
                  shaped by natural selection, is an adaptation to multiniche
                  environments, and involves an integration of genetic
                  influences and condition-sensitivity.},
  keywords     = {Stress reactivity; Stress physiology; Ontogeny; Evolutionary
                  psychology; Phenotypic plasticity; Molecular genetics;
