  abstract     = {Hemiballism is a rare movement disorder that presents with
                  unilateral flinging movements of the limbs. In traditional
                  teaching, it has been characterised as almost pathognomonic of
                  a lesion in the subthalamic nucleus (STN). The prognosis was
                  described as grave, with severe disability and death in many
                  cases. However, review of more recent reports shows that the
                  STN is directly involved in only a minority of cases. The
