                  Oeberst, and Augustin (2004) proposed a descriptive
                  information-processing model of the components that integrate
                  an aesthetic episode. This theory offered explanations for
                  modern art's large number of individualized styles,
                  innovativeness, and for the diverse aesthetic experiences it
                  can stimulate. In addition, it described how information is
                  processed over the time course of an aesthetic episode, within
                  and over perceptual, cognitive and emotional components. Here,
