               powerful theory of how the human brain works, explaining why
               computers are not intelligent and how, based on this new theory,
               we can finally build intelligent machines.The brain is not a
               computer, but a memory system that stores experiences in a way
               that reflects the true structure of the world, remembering
               sequences of events and their nested relationships and making
               predictions based on those memories. It is this memory-prediction
               system that forms the basis of intelligence, perception,
               creativity, and even consciousness.In an engaging style that will
               captivate audiences from the merely curious to the professional
