               impacts of rising consumption. Unless we can radically lower the
               environmental impact of economic activity – and there is no
               evidence to suggest that we can – we will have to devise a path
               to prosperity that does not rely on continued growth. Economic
               heresy? Or an opportunity to improve the sources of well-being,
               creativity and lasting prosperity that lie outside the realm of
               the market? Tim Jackson provides a credible vision of how human
               society can flourish within the ecological limits of a finite
               planet. Fulfilling this vision is simply the most urgent task of
