  date         = {2010-03-15},
  abstract     = {A small proportion of patients with Parkinson's disease (PD)
                  develop a dopamine dysregulation syndrome (DDS). Management of
                  such patients can be difficult; hence, early identification
                  and careful monitoring of at-risk individuals are important.
                  Based on four illustrative cases, we wish to draw attention to
                  the risk of developing DDS in PD patients engaged in a
