  date      = {2017},
  abstract  = {Race was once thought to be a real biological concept when
               anthropologists used study of the human skull as a way to justify
               racial differences and social inequality. Scientists no longer
               believe there is a biological basis to distinguish racial groups,
               rather, race is a social, cultural, and/or political construct
               wherein racial segregation has real consequences on health and
               health disparities. The biological basis of differential
               prevalence of disease susceptibility or resistance is due to
               genetic variations that exist in various racial and ethnic
               groups. Thus, race as a social concept can be used to categorize
               populations or groups based on disease susceptibility or
