  date         = {2021-12-13},
  abstract     = {Interest in the direct interactions between individual people
                  and nature has grown rapidly. This attention encompasses
                  multiple academic disciplines and practical perspectives. A
                  central challenge thus lies in creating a rich
                  cross-disciplinary understanding of these interactions, rather
                  than one that might become characterized by little conceptual,
                  terminological and methodological unity. Here, to facilitate
                  the former outcome, we bring together concepts and theories
                  about direct human–nature interactions drawn from diverse
                  disciplines within a unified conceptual framework. Using this
                  framework, we discuss the linkages among key concepts and
                  theories, identify important knowledge gaps and suggest
