  pages        = {669--678},
  date         = {2013-12},
  abstract     = {The machine conception of the organism (MCO) is one of the
                  most pervasive notions in modern biology. However, it has not
                  yet received much attention by philosophers of biology. The
                  MCO has its origins in Cartesian natural philosophy, and it is
                  based on the metaphorical redescription of the organism as a
