                  stimulation at bilateral ventral subthalamic nucleus on
                  emotional processing in PD patients using an affective task,
                  compared to that of clinical-frequency stimulation and
                  off-stimulation. METHODS: Twenty PD patients with bilateral
                  subthalamic deep brain stimulation for more than six months
                  were tested with the affective task under three stimulation
                  conditions (10Hz, 130Hz, and off-stimulation) in a
                  double-blinded randomized design. RESULTS: While 130Hz
                  stimulation reduced arousal ratings in all patients, 10Hz
                  stimulation increased arousal selectively in patients with
