  pages        = {1259--1272},
  date         = {2023-08-21},
  abstract     = {BACKGROUND: Deep brain stimulation of the subcallosal
                  cingulate area (SCC-DBS) is a promising neuromodulatory
                  therapy for treatment-resistant depression (TRD). Biomarkers
                  of optimal target engagement are needed to guide surgical
                  targeting and stimulation parameter selection and to reduce
                  variance in clinical outcome. OBJECTIVE/HYPOTHESIS: We aimed
                  to characterize the relationship between stimulation location,
                  white matter tract engagement, and clinical outcome in a large
                  (n = 60) TRD cohort treated with SCC-DBS. A smaller cohort (n
