  pages        = {726--744},
  date         = {2023-08},
  abstract     = {Brain development is underpinned by complex interactions
                  between neural assemblies, driving structural and functional
                  change. This neuroconstructivism (the notion that neural
                  functions are shaped by these interactions) is core to some
                  developmental theories. However, due to their complexity,
                  understanding underlying developmental mechanisms is
                  challenging. Elsewhere in neurobiology, a computational
                  revolution has shown that mathematical models of hidden
