                  cognition (P < 0.01) and activities of daily living (P =
                  0.01). Excellent responders had higher challenge doses (P =
                  0.03) and were more likely to be on combination therapy (P <
                  0.01). CONCLUSION: Three distinct patterns of the dopaminergic
                  response were observed. As the proportion of PD cases with
                  definite dopa responsiveness increased over time, the initial
                  treatment response may be an unreliable diagnostic aid.},
