                  obsessive–compulsive disorder have demonstrated direct
                  involvement of axonal fibres rather than grey matter. In this
                  Review, we draw on clinical and experimental data to examine
                  the various hypotheses that have been put forward to explain
                  the effects of DBS. In agreement with several other experts,
