                  manifestations of HD vary widely and sometimes have an
                  atypical onset. In this paper we primarily sought information
                  on affected patients who initially presented with movement
                  disorders other than chorea. We also investigated atypical
                  motor presentations in relation to triplet CAG expansions.
                  After reviewing the clinical records of two neurological
                  centres, we identified patients with a final, documented
