                  processes to model them. Within predictive coding theory,
                  oscillatory beta-band activity has been linked to top-down
                  predictive signals and gamma-band activity to bottom-up
                  prediction errors. However, neurocognitive evidence for
                  predictive coding outside lower-level sensory areas is scarce.
