                  Despite the changes, the alpha1 subunit content of
                  Golgi-cell-to-granule-cell synapses in alpha6 -/- animals
                  remained unaltered, as did the frequency of alpha1
                  immunopositive synapses in the glomeruli. Furthermore, no
                  change was apparent in the expression of the alpha1, beta2 and
                  gamma2 subunits in Purkinje cells and interneurons of the
                  molecular layer. These results demonstrate that in alpha6 -/-
                  mice, the cerebellum expresses only half of the number of
