  abstract     = {Rapid onset dystonia-parkinsonism (RDP) is a rare movement
                  disorder with autosomal dominant inheritance, characterised by
                  sudden onset of dystonic spasms and slowness of movement. To
                  date, three families have been described that share linkage to
                  the same location on chromosome 19q13, designated DYT12. Very
                  recently, mutations in the ATP1A3 gene at the DYT12 locus have
                  been demonstrated in seven unrelated patients, including the
                  three previously linked families. A large RDP family is
                  reported here, with eight definitely and one possibly affected
                  members, that is not linked to the DYT12 region and has no
                  mutation in the ATP1A3 gene. Predominant cranial-cervical
