  journaltitle = {Stroke and Vascular Neurology},
  volume       = {2},
  issue        = {4},
  pages        = {230--243},
  date         = {2017},
  abstract     = {Artificial intelligence (AI) aims to mimic human cognitive
                  functions. It is bringing a paradigm shift to healthcare,
                  powered by increasing availability of healthcare data and
                  rapid progress of analytics techniques. We survey the current
                  status of AI applications in healthcare and discuss its
                  future. AI can be applied to various types of healthcare data
                  (structured and unstructured). Popular AI techniques include
                  machine learning methods for structured data, such as the
                  classical support vector machine and neural network, and the
                  modern deep learning, as well as natural language processing
                  for unstructured data. Major disease areas that use AI tools
