  date         = {2015-07-03},
  abstract     = {Planners making groundwater plans often use scientific
                  hydrological forecasts to estimate long term the risk of water
                  depletion. We study a group of Chicago planners and
                  stakeholders who learned to use and helped develop agent-based
                  models (ABM) of coupled land-use change and groundwater flow,
