  issue        = {1},
  pages        = {82--98},
  date         = {2012},
  abstract     = {This paper presents a theoretical review of rapid eye movement
                  sleep with a special focus on pontine-geniculate-occipital
                  waves and what they might tell us about the functional anatomy
                  of sleep and consciousness. In particular, we review
                  established ideas about the nature and purpose of sleep in
