  date         = {2018},
  abstract     = {Today, the basal ganglia (BG) network can be viewed as a
                  three-layer neural network in which the striatum and the
                  subthalamic nucleus (STN) are the two BG input structures and
                  together innervate BG downstream structures using GABA and
                  glutamate, respectively. The striatum is larger than the STN
