  date         = {2019},
  abstract     = {Real‐life observational report of clinical efficacy of
                  bilateral subthalamic stimulation (STN‐DBS), apomorphine
                  (APO), and intrajejunal levodopa infusion (IJLI) on quality of
                  life, motor, and nonmotor symptoms (NMS) in Parkinson's
                  disease (PD). In this prospective, multicenter, international,
                  real‐life cohort observation study of 173 PD patients
                  undergoing STN‐DBS (n = 101), IJLI (n = 33), or APO (n = 39)
