  date         = {2015},
  abstract     = {Exposure to news, opinion, and civic information increasingly
                  occurs through social media. How do these online networks
                  influence exposure to perspectives that cut across ideological
                  lines? Using deidentified data, we examined how 10.1 million
                  U.S. Facebook users interact with socially shared news. We
                  directly measured ideological homophily in friend networks and
                  examined the extent to which heterogeneous friends could
                  potentially expose individuals to cross-cutting content. We
                  then quantified the extent to which individuals encounter
