  date         = {2021-11-24},
  abstract     = {Interpersonal synchrony is a fundamental part of human social
                  interaction, with known effects on facilitating social
                  bonding. Moving in time with another person facilitates
                  prosocial behaviour, however, it is unknown if the degree of
                  synchronisation predicts the degree of social bonding.
