                  horizons and subsequently the situational context on the
                  macrolayer are defined by the complex affordances of a
                  situation on a personal or interpersonal level. On both time
                  layers, cognition can be defined as a continuous dynamic
                  process, reflecting the transition from one situated state to
                  another. Taken together, the events forming the delimiting
                  horizons of these situations correspond to the temporal
