  pages        = {242--248},
  date         = {2013-10},
  abstract     = {One well accepted functional feature of the parkinsonian state
                  is the recording of enhanced beta oscillatory activity in the
                  basal ganglia. This has been demonstrated in patients with
                  Parkinson's disease (PD) and in animal models such as the rat
                  with 6-hydroxydopamine (6-OHDA)-induced lesion and
