                  noise-based mechanisms can lead to conservatism, the Bayesian
                  likelihood bias, illusory correlations, biased self-other
                  placement, subadditivity, exaggerated expectation, the
                  confidence bias, and the hard-easy effect. Analytical tools
                  from information theory are used to explore the nature and
                  limitations that characterize such information processes for
                  binary and multiary decision-making exercises. The ensuing
