  pages        = {2633--2683},
  date         = {2017-10},
  abstract     = {This article offers a formal account of curiosity and insight
                  in terms of active (Bayesian) inference. It deals with the
                  dual problem of inferring states of the world and learning its
                  statistical structure. In contrast to current trends in
                  machine learning (e.g., deep learning), we focus on how people
