                  and one probe tone of randomly selected frequencies. Within
                  each cycle, the three prime tones remained identical while the
                  probe tones changed once at some point (e.g., from repetition
                  of 123X to repetition of 123Y). Therefore, the repetition of
                  probe tones can reveal the development of perceptual
                  inferences in low and high precision contexts depending on
