                  subunit-containing GABARs. Based on data and a simple
                  theoretical analysis, we estimate that the average
                  extrasynaptic [GABA] is ∼160 nm in perfused slices. These
                  results (1) demonstrate contributions of α6 subunits to both
                  synaptic and extrasynaptic GABA responses, (2) establish that
                  δ subunit-containing GABARs are benzodiazepine sensitive at
