  issue        = {2},
  pages        = {700--708},
  date         = {2006-02},
  abstract     = {Noradrenaline (NA) modulates synaptic transmission in various
                  sites of the CNS. In the cerebellar cortex, several studies
                  have revealed that NA enhances inhibitory synaptic
                  transmission by beta-adrenoceptor-and cyclic AMP-dependent
                  pathways. However, the effects of alpha-adrenoceptor
