                  model (a Bayes-optimal decision-making agent) to perform a
                  simple task involving social and non-social inferences. We
                  show that even moderate changes in some model parameters -
                  decreasing confidence in sensory input and increasing
                  confidence in states implied by its own (especially habitual)
