                  specifically in the social domain. The model also reproduces
                  some classic psychological effects, including choice-induced
                  preference change, and an optimism bias in inferences about
                  oneself. A key observation is that no change in a single
                  parameter is both necessary and sufficient for delusions;
                  rather, delusions arise due to conditional dependencies that
                  create 'basins of attraction' which trap Bayesian beliefs.
