  date         = {2018-03-01},
  abstract     = {The historical debate on representation in cognitive science
                  and neuroscience construes representations as theoretical
                  posits and discusses the degree to which we have reason to
                  posit them. We reject the premise of that debate. We argue
                  that experimental neuroscientists routinely observe and
                  manipulate neural representations in their laboratory.
