  pages        = {3573--3589},
  date         = {2020-05-18},
  abstract     = {Choosing actions that result in advantageous outcomes is a
                  fundamental function of nervous systems. All computational
                  decision-making models contain a mechanism that controls the
                  variability of (or confidence in) action selection, but its
                  neural implementation is unclear-especially in humans. We
