  date         = {2016-07},
  abstract     = {Difficulties in set-shifting are commonly reported in both
                  autism spectrum disorder (ASD) and anorexia nervosa (AN)
                  populations. Despite this, it is not known whether this
                  cognitive profile persists across different ages, or whether
                  the profiles seen in ASD and AN are comparable. This
