                  -0.05 to 0.55, z = 1.66, p = 0.096). Meta-regression indicated
                  no effect of diagnosis (AN or ASD) on performance in adult
                  studies but there was a non-significant trend (p = 0.053)
                  towards children with ASD performing worse than children with
                  AN. While difficulties with set-shifting appear to be stable
                  in ASD, there may be differences between children and adults
                  with AN, which warrant further investigation.},
