  pages        = {1898--1902},
  date         = {2003-03-21},
  abstract     = {Uncertainty is critical in the measure of information and in
                  assessing the accuracy of predictions. It is determined by
                  probability P, being maximal at P = 0.5 and decreasing at
                  higher and lower probabilities. Using distinct stimuli to
                  indicate the probability of reward, we found that the phasic
