                  highlighted consumption trends resulting from the virus
                  outbreak, very few studies explore how the current pandemic
                  challenges consumption. Three trends are identified: the
                  downsizing of consumption, emergence of anti-globalization
                  sentiments, and negative consumer reactions to the misconduct
                  of brands/companies. First, the lockdown was an opportunity
                  for people to test a simpler lifestyle by reducing their level
                  of consumption, having realized that over-consumption does not
                  make them happy and questioned its negative impact on the
                  environment. Second, the pandemic may reinforce
                  anti-globalization ideas, leading consumers to move away from
