  pages        = {548--553},
  date         = {2015-07-07},
  abstract     = {Anthropogenic climate change will have significant impacts on
                  both human migration and population health, including
                  infectious disease. It will amplify and alter migration
                  pathways, and will contribute to the changing ecology and
                  transmission dynamics of infectious disease. However there has
                  been limited consideration of the intersections between
                  migration and health in the context of a changing climate.
