                  cognitive functions. A dynamical model constrained by
                  connectivity data sheds insight into the experimentally
                  observed signatures of frequency-dependent Granger causality
                  for feedforward versus feedback signaling. Concerted
                  experiments capitalizing on recent technical advances and
                  combining tract-tracing, high-resolution fMRI, optogenetics
                  and mathematical modeling hold the promise of a much improved
                  understanding of lamina-constrained mechanisms of neural
