                  with PD and 15 individuals without PD in order to gauge their
                  subjective impressions and valuations of music. Participants
                  completed The Brief Music Experience Questionnaire (BMEQ), a
                  standard self-report measure pertaining to the role of music
                  in one's life, prior to performing a perception task which
                  involved listening to and making sound adjustments to three
                  music recordings. Following the perception task, a custom Exit
                  Survey was administered to evaluate the experience of
                  listening to and engaging with the music in the perception
                  task. In all six dimensions of the BMEQ, examining aspects of
                  music experience including commitment to music, self-reported
                  musical aptitude, social uplift, affective reactions, positive
                  psychotropic effects, and reactive musical behavior (RMB,
                  pertaining to actions or behaviors in response to music), the
