  issue        = {1},
  pages        = {4190},
  date         = {2017-06-23},
  abstract     = {Electroencephalographic hyperscanning was used to investigate
                  interbrain synchronization patterns in dyads of participants
                  interacting through speech. Results show that brain
                  oscillations are synchronized between listener and speaker
                  during oral narratives. This interpersonal synchronization is
                  mediated in part by a lower-level sensory mechanism of
