  issue        = {11},
  pages        = {2968--2981},
  date         = {2017-11-01},
  abstract     = {Exaggerated basal ganglia beta activity (13-35 Hz) is commonly
                  found in patients with Parkinson's disease and can be
                  suppressed by dopaminergic medication, with the degree of
                  suppression being correlated with the improvement in motor
                  symptoms. Importantly, beta activity is not continuously
