                  between structures in the basal ganglia-cortical network. The
                  impact of this is greater during long as opposed to short
                  duration beta bursts. Accordingly, we posit that episodes of
                  simultaneously elevated coupling across multiple structures in
                  the basal ganglia-cortical circuit further limit information
                  coding capacity and may have further impact upon motor
                  impairment.},
  keywords     = {Parkinson's disease; Beta oscillations; Basal ganglia-cortical
