  pages        = {147--163},
  date         = {2018-08},
  abstract     = {Enactive approaches to cognitive science aim to explain human
                  cognitive processes across the board without making any appeal
                  to internal, content-carrying representational states. A
                  challenge to such a research programme in cognitive science
                  that immediately arises is how to explain cognition in
                  so-called 'representation-hungry' domains. Examples of
