                  differentially predicted by auditory cues. Critically, the
                  predictive strengths of cues varied over time, requiring
                  subjects to continuously update estimates of stimulus
                  probabilities. This online inference, modeled using a
                  hierarchical Bayesian learner, was reflected behaviorally:
                  speed and accuracy of motor responses increased significantly
                  with predictability of the stimuli.We used nonlinear dynamic
