                  social cohesion, reciprocity, and reward. While most musicians
                  involved in collective forms of musicking already have some
                  familiarity with these terms and their associated experiences,
                  we currently lack an analytical vocabulary to approach them in
                  a more targeted way. To fill this gap, we adopt insights from
                  these frameworks to suggest that musical participation may be
                  advantageously characterized as an open, non-equilibrium,
