                  This brain region overlaps with the inferior frontal gyrus,
                  the frontal eye field, and the dorsolateral prefrontal cortex,
                  which are implicated in inference of mental states and social
                  cognition. Our result demonstrates the adverse effect of
                  parenting stress on mother-child attunement that is evident at
                  a brain-to-brain level. Mother-child brain-to-brain asynchrony
                  may underlie the robust association between parenting stress
                  and poor dyadic co-regulation. We anticipate our study to form
