  abstract     = {The free energy principle, an influential framework in
                  computational neuroscience and theoretical neurobiology,
                  starts from the assumption that living systems ensure adaptive
                  exchanges with their environment by minimizing the objective
                  function of variational free energy. Following this premise,
                  it claims to deliver a promising integration of the life
                  sciences. In recent work, Markov Blankets, one of the central
                  constructs of the free energy principle, have been applied to
                  resolve debates central to philosophy (such as demarcating the
