  abstract     = {Scientific realism holds that scientific theories are
                  approximations of universal truths about reality, whereas
                  scientific instrumentalism posits that scientific theories are
                  intellectual structures that provide adequate predictions of
                  what is observed and useful frameworks for answering questions
                  and solving problems in a given domain. These philosophical
