  abstract     = {Scientists have developed hundreds of techniques to measure
                  the interactions between pairs of processes in complex
                  systems. But these computational methods -- from correlation
                  coefficients to causal inference -- rely on distinct
                  quantitative theories that remain largely disconnected. Here
                  we introduce a library of 249 statistics for pairwise
                  interactions and assess their behavior on 1053 multivariate
                  time series from a wide range of real-world and
