                  dynamics. Thus, the ability of a single neuron to minimize
                  surprise—that is, the difference between actual and expected
                  activity—could be an important missing element to understand
                  computation in the brain. In artificial neural networks, a
                  typical neuron generally performs a simple summation of
                  inputs. Using computational and electrophysiological data, the
