  pages        = {177--183},
  date         = {2010-02},
  abstract     = {Art is a uniquely human activity associated fundamentally with
                  symbolic and abstract cognition. Its practice in human
                  societies throughout the world, coupled with seeming
                  non-functionality, has led to three major brain theories of
                  art. (1) The localized brain regions and pathways theory links
                  art to multiple neural regions. (2) The display of art and its
                  aesthetics theory is tied to the biological motivation of
