                  unstable modular assignments correlated significantly with the
                  pattern of expression of subclasses of noradrenergic and
                  cholinergic receptors across the cerebral cortex. Altogether,
                  these findings demonstrate that cognitive fluctuations are
                  associated with an imaging signature of dynamic network
                  impairment linked to specific
                  neurotransmitters/neuromodulators within the ascending arousal
                  system, highlighting novel potential diagnostic and
                  therapeutic approaches for this troubling symptom.},
  language     = {en}
}

