               DBS treatment. While a review of the literature and meta-analyses
               indicate DBS for movement disorders to be safe from a
               neurobehavioral standpoint it is also clear that a small subset
               of patients have experienced moderate or severe neurobehavioral
               morbidity. If one combines the various cognitive and psychiatric
               morbidities reported across studies, approximately 10\% of
               patients with PD undergoing DBS have experienced one or another
               neurobehavioral adverse events. Furthermore, several small
               studies have indicated that improvements in motor symptoms and
