  pages        = {435--445},
  date         = {2008-03},
  abstract     = {There is scientific consensus that the global climate is
                  changing, with rising surface temperatures, melting ice and
                  snow, rising sea levels, and increasing climate variability.
                  These changes are expected to have substantial impacts on
                  human health. There are known, effective public health
                  responses for many of these impacts, but the scope, timeline,
