  abstract     = {The purpose of this study was to determine punding prevalence
                  in an ambulatory Parkinson's disease (PD) population. We
                  conducted a patient-and-caregiver-completed punding survey in
                  373 consecutive patients in an academic ambulatory center.
                  Completion rate was 78\%. Only four patients were identified
                  as punding. Patients did not retain insight to their behavior.
                  Forty patients with high-dose levodopa monotherapy or levodopa
                  and dopamine agonist treatment had physician-administered
                  interview. None had punding. Punding incidence was low in this
                  patient group (1.4\%) in contrast with previous reports of
