  issue        = {1},
  pages        = {65--85},
  date         = {2001},
  abstract     = {The activity of midbrain dopamine neurons is strikingly
                  similar to the reward prediction error of temporal difference
                  reinforcement learning models. Experimental evidence and
                  simulation studies suggest that dopamine neuron activity
                  serves as an effective reinforcement signal for learning of
                  sensorimotor associations in striatal matrisomes. In the
