                  temporal difference model does not form novel associative
                  chains. Transient membrane effects of the dopamine-like signal
                  on striatal firing substantially shorten the reaction time in
                  the planning task. The capability for planning is improved by
                  influences of dopamine on the durations of membrane potential
                  fluctuations and by manipulations that prolong the reaction
                  time of the model. These results suggest that responses of
                  dopamine neurons to conditioned stimuli contribute to
