                  anatomical and physiological characteristics of basal
                  ganglia-thalamocortical connectivity and suggests that the
                  basal ganglia performs reinforcement-biased dimensionality
                  reduction of cortical inputs. We further suggest that since
                  such selective encoding may bias the representation at the
                  level of the frontal cortex towards the selection of rewarded
                  plans and actions, the reinforcement-driven dimensionality
                  reduction framework may serve as a basis for basal ganglia
                  actor models. We conclude with a short discussion of the dual
                  role of the dopamine signal in RL and in behavioral switching.},
