  pages        = {541--574},
  date         = {2010-04},
  abstract     = {The basal ganglia play a central role in cognition and are
                  involved in such general functions as action selection and
                  reinforcement learning. Here, we present a model exploring the
                  hypothesis that the basal ganglia implement a conditional
                  information-routing system. The system directs the
                  transmission of cortical signals between pairs of regions by
                  manipulating separately the selection of sources and
                  destinations of information transfers. We suggest that such a
                  mechanism provides an account for several cognitive functions
