                  spiking neurons that implements in detail the thalamo-cortical
                  circuits that are believed to be involved in action learning
                  and execution. A key feature of this model is that neurons are
                  organized in small pools in the motor cortex and form
                  independent loops with specific pools of the basal ganglia
                  where inhibitory circuits implement a multistep selection
                  mechanism. The described model has been validated utilizing it
