  pages        = {116--130},
  date         = {2018-01-01},
  abstract     = {Synchrony between local field potential (LFP) rhythms is
                  thought to boost the signal of attended sensory inputs. Other
                  cognitive functions could benefit from such gain control. One
                  is categorization where decisions can be difficult if
                  categories differ in subtle ways. Monkeys were trained to
