  pages        = {560--573},
  date         = {2010-05-21},
  abstract     = {Punding is a stereotyped behavior characterized by an intense
                  fascination with a complex, excessive, nongoal oriented,
                  repetitive activity. Men tend to repetitively tinker with
                  technical equipment such as radio sets, clocks, watches and
                  car engines, the parts of which may be analyzed, arranged,
