  pages        = {160},
  date         = {2016-04-26},
  abstract     = {The last decade has witnessed a renaissance of empirical and
                  psychological approaches to art study, especially regarding
                  cognitive models of art processing experience. This new
                  emphasis on modeling has often become the basis for our
                  theoretical understanding of human interaction with art.
                  Models also often define areas of focus and hypotheses for new
