  pages        = {44},
  date         = {2022-04-19},
  abstract     = {Adaptive deep brain stimulation (aDBS) is a promising concept
                  for feedback-based neurostimulation, with the potential of
                  clinical implementation with the sensing-enabled Percept
                  neurostimulator. We aim to characterize chronic
                  electrophysiological activity during stimulation and to
                  validate beta-band activity as a biomarker for bradykinesia.
                  Subthalamic activity was recorded during stepwise stimulation
                  amplitude increase OFF medication in 10 Parkinson's patients
                  during rest and finger tapping. Offline analysis of
                  wavelet-transformed beta-band activity and assessment of
                  inter-variable relationships in linear mixed effects models
                  were implemented. There was a stepwise suppression of low-beta
