                  Yigit and Rosskopf, Johannes and Kloth, Christopher},
  journaltitle = {Diagnostics (Basel)},
  publisher    = {MDPI AG},
  volume       = {13},
  issue        = {3},
  pages        = {447},
  date         = {2023-01-26},
  abstract     = {The imaging evaluation of computed tomography (CT), CT
                  angiography (CTA), and CT perfusion (CTP) is of crucial
                  importance in the setting of each emergency department for
                  suspected cerebrovascular impairment. A fast and clear
                  assignment of characteristic imaging findings of acute stroke
                  and its differential diagnoses is essential for every
                  radiologist. Different entities can mimic clinical signs of an
                  acute stroke, thus the knowledge and fast identification of
