                  receptive field of the neuron, and patterns detected on basal
                  and apical dendrites act as predictions by slightly
                  depolarizing the neuron without generating an action
                  potential. By this mechanism, a neuron can predict its
                  activation in hundreds of independent contexts. We then
                  present a network model based on neurons with these properties
                  that learns time-based sequences. The network relies on fast
