  journaltitle = {Neurol. Sci.},
  date         = {2022-05-05},
  abstract     = {OBJECTIVE: Restless legs syndrome (RLS) is known to be
                  associated with multiple sclerosis (MS) and may be caused by
                  MS lesions in specific cerebral brain regions. Applying a
                  voxel-wise lesion analysis, we tried to identify the
                  contribution of cerebral MS lesions to RLS. METHODS: In this
