                  and Ritter, Petra},
  journaltitle = {Exp. Neurol.},
  volume       = {354},
  pages        = {114111},
  date         = {2022-05-13},
  abstract     = {Deep brain stimulation (DBS) has been successfully applied in
                  various neurodegenerative diseases as an effective symptomatic
                  treatment. However, its mechanisms of action within the brain
                  network are still poorly understood. Many virtual DBS models
                  analyze a subnetwork around the basal ganglia and its dynamics
