  pages        = {672--680},
  date         = {2020-08},
  abstract     = {BACKGROUND: Deep brain stimulation (DBS) improves motor
                  symptoms and quality of life in patients with Parkinson's
                  disease (PD) and early motor complications, suggesting that
                  DBS could be prescribed to the working-age PD population.
                  OBJECTIVES: To investigate the effect of DBS compared with
