                  results elucidate potential substrates of GP functional
                  dichotomy, and emphasise that rhythmic inputs from striatum,
                  thalamus and cortex are important for setting activity in the
                  STN-GP network during Parkinsonian beta oscillations,
                  suggesting they arise from interactions between most nodes of
                  basal ganglia-thalamocortical circuits.},
