  pages        = {9--18},
  date         = {2019-04},
  abstract     = {The prolonged reaction times seen in Parkinson's disease (PD)
                  have been linked to a dopaminergic-dependent deficit in using
                  prior information to prepare responses, but also have been
                  explained by an altered temporal processing. However, an
                  underlying cognitive mechanism linking dopamine, temporal
