                  Farmer, Simon F},
  journaltitle = {J. Neurophysiol.},
  volume       = {119},
  issue        = {5},
  pages        = {1608--1628},
  date         = {2018-05-01},
  abstract     = {Much of the motor impairment associated with Parkinson's
                  disease is thought to arise from pathological activity in the
                  networks formed by the basal ganglia (BG) and motor cortex. To
                  evaluate several hypotheses proposed to explain the emergence
                  of pathological oscillations in parkinsonism, we investigated
                  changes to the directed connectivity in BG networks following
