                  with a particular focus on the frontal lobotomy. The
                  transition to the modern era of psychosurgery is discussed, as
                  well as the neurobiology underlying current psychosurgical
                  procedures. The techniques of stereotactic cingulotomy,
                  capsulotomy, subcaudate tractotomy, and limbic leukotomy are
                  described, as well their indications and side effects. Due to
