  pages        = {2022.07.22.501193},
  date         = {2022-07-23},
  abstract     = {Biomarkers of behavior and psychiatric illness for cognitive
                  and clinical neuroscience remain out of reach[1][1]–[4][2].
                  Suboptimal reliability of biological measurements, such as
                  functional magnetic resonance imaging (fMRI), is increasingly
                  cited as a primary culprit for discouragingly large sample
