  volume       = {8},
  pages        = {427},
  date         = {2017-03-29},
  abstract     = {In this paper, we show that a neurally implemented a cognitive
                  architecture with evolutionary dynamics can solve the
                  four-tree problem. Our model, called Darwinian Neurodynamics,
                  assumes that the unconscious mechanism of problem solving
                  during insight tasks is a Darwinian process. It is based on
                  the evolution of patterns that represent candidate solutions
                  to a problem, and are stored and reproduced by a population of
                  attractor networks. In our first experiment, we used human
