                  F and Ganos, Christos and Hallett, Mark and Starr, Philip A
                  and Ostrem, Jill L and Wu, Yiwen and Zhang, Chencheng and Fox,
                  Michael D and Horn, Andreas},
  journaltitle = {bioRxiv},
  date         = {2024-05-25},
  abstract     = {AbstractDeep brain stimulation is a viable and efficacious
                  treatment option for dystonia. While the internal pallidum
                  serves as the primary target, more recently, stimulation of
                  the subthalamic nucleus (STN) has been investigated. However,
                  optimal targeting within this structure and its complex
